From: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] MLD: Handle MTK station association events

MTK driver manages MLO station links without reporting standard nl80211
link information. Association request and response IEs provide the MLD
addresses, requested links and per-link security parameters needed by
wpa_supplicant to process EAPOL-Key messages.

These IEs establish private MLO security state for SAE associations.
PMKSA caching can skip SAE external authentication, so association state
cannot depend on a new external authentication exchange. When that
exchange is present, its MLD addresses must match the association IEs.

APCLI netdevs use link MAC addresses, which can differ from the local
MLD address. PTK derivation and MAC Address KDEs use the MLD address,
while MLO Link KDEs describe individual link addresses.

wpa_supplicant validates link profiles before installing security
parameters and selects each group key's link through the MTK preset-link
command. Private association state is cleared on disconnect so subsequent
connections cannot reuse stale link information.

Signed-off-by: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
